# ✋ Welcome to the service agent python-fastapi

Some of the things this agent provides for you:

## Developer Experience
- uv (use `uv add <package>` to add a new package; `uv add --dev <package>` for dev deps)
- hot-reload
- auto-generation of OpenAPI documentation

## Code
- OpenAPI

## Production ready
- Dockerfile and verifiable build plan generation (requires `output_directory`); the CLI owns image builds, builder selection, caching, and publishing
- Kubernetes deployment

## Declared container health

Kubernetes probes follow the authored REST endpoint's health predicates and transport. HTTP checks preserve accepted statuses and bounded body containment; redirects are not followed. Secured container-local checks authenticate the listener against the exact certificate mounted at `UVICORN_SSL_CERTFILE` before sending HTTP data. The isolated Python probe imports no application code and emits no response content or certificate material.

Startup, readiness and liveness are separate policies. The current Core Kubernetes manifest profile requires all three, so deployment refuses absent startup/liveness declarations instead of copying readiness into a restart policy. New scaffolds explicitly declare `/version` readiness and transport startup/liveness. Existing services must author their own policies. Whole-second timing is required by Kubernetes; predicates or additional listener health that this agent cannot preserve are refused rather than silently omitted.

Image SBOM requests must provide immutable subjects and their registry/daemon source. The Core scanner preserves each requested identity; there is no registry-to-daemon fallback for a different image.
